    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-14420",
      "problem": "What number is missing from the division problem below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/cf2500f82f337e5635a5ca9854579e3b883f42cde4598d4324c94364bf998a0d.png)",
      "worked_solution": "We have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{15}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/ed5517a9242aed1c5b521ca07772dacbb7c96a73c69d4d9c6214a098742358e2.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $5$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $5$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5.$",
